<title>FINLAND: Foreign ownership in Finnish companies down in Dec.</title>
<headline>Foreign ownership in Finnish companies down in Dec.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Foreign ownership of Finnish firms registered in the Central Share Register (OKR) fell to 26.9 percent of shares at end-December from 27.2 at end- November, OKR said in a review distributed on Tuesday evening.</p>
<p>Foreign ownership of building materials and cargo equipment group Partek fell to 31.8 percent from 34.7 percent at end-November.</p>
<p>Foreign share ownership in telecom group Nokia was down only marginally to 70.66 percent from 70.69 percent.</p>
<p>Foreign holdings in office furniture group Martela bucked the trend, rising to 41.8 percent from 35.9.</p>
